(7479608, 1189283, 20056, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your comments but I am not convinced of going in the direction You both mention... Is something like this what You are referring to? <a href="//photo.net/photodb/photo?photo_id=18300171&amp;size=lg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//photo.net/photodb/photo?photo_id=18300171&amp;size=lg</a></td>', 'Thanks for your comments but I am not convinced of going in the direction You both mention... Is something like this what You are referring to? //photo.net/photodb/photo?photo_id=18300171&size=lg', '2016-10-26 09:54:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(7479620, 1189451, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>Youre definitely tugging at my heart strings with scene Eugene, having spent 15 years living on a narrow boat I wondered why I didnt recognise this property but the Llangollen was one of the few canals I couldnt get the boat up. Anyway, enough of me, youre right there is only one composition possible because it works so well though I think I would have cropped the right between the chimneys in favour of more of the left, the natural part of the scene. As it is the house and the white rendering are very dominant and given the challenge brief you would have been able to display more foliage which may also have increased your score and voter participation. Thanks for your welcome reminder of many pleasant years past.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge Youre definitely tugging at my heart strings with scene Eugene, having spent 15 years living on a narrow boat I wondered why I didnt recognise this property but the Llangollen was one of the few canals I couldnt get the boat up. Anyway, enough of me, youre right there is only one composition possible because it works so well though I think I would have cropped the right between the chimneys in favour of more of the left, the natural part of the scene. As it is the house and the white rendering are very dominant and given the challenge brief you would have been able to display more foliage which may also have increased your score and voter participation. Thanks for your welcome reminder of many pleasant years past.', '2016-10-26 13:07:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(7479622, 1189387, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>I can see why this appealed to you, well observed Marcel. I like the concept and observation but the blue of that sky is just too dominant. I dont think you needed to include all of the building in fact by cropping out the top half of the image the message that the scene is past its best comes through much stronger, Im looking at this scrolled up to a level just below the gantry entering from the left and it works much better for me. Try it, see what you think?</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that meets the challenge I can see why this appealed to you, well observed Marcel. I like the concept and observation but the blue of that sky is just too dominant. I dont think you needed to include all of the building in fact by cropping out the top half of the image the message that the scene is past its best comes through much stronger, Im looking at this scrolled up to a level just below the gantry entering from the left and it works much better for me. Try it, see what you think?', '2016-10-26 13:16:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7479623, 1189424, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>I can see why this appealed to you, Fabio it certainly fills the challenge brief of foliage. The foliage is well lit and the scene naturally draws you into the tunnel of foliage. The grass is somewhat saturated and would benefit from easing back a bit to stop it dominating the image in favour of the foliage. A good attempt, thanks for sharing it with us</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that meets the challenge I can see why this appealed to you, Fabio it certainly fills the challenge brief of foliage. The foliage is well lit and the scene naturally draws you into the tunnel of foliage. The grass is somewhat saturated and would benefit from easing back a bit to stop it dominating the image in favour of the foliage. A good attempt, thanks for sharing it with us', '2016-10-26 13:21:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(7479628, 1189453, 50864, '<td valign="top">I meant to come back and comment. So interesting, different and beautiful.</td>', 'I meant to come back and comment. So interesting, different and beautiful.', '2016-10-26 14:25:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(7479650, 1189236, 69684, '<td valign="top">It''s a good thing you''re mobile again!</td>', 'It''s a good thing you''re mobile again!', '2016-10-26 17:20:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(7479651, 1189330, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>Ooh thats nice were my words aloud as soon as it appeared! What a wonderful time of year this is, its colours and textures just have to be exploited to the full and your image does just that. I like the frame-filling aspect but its those lovely vibrant colours that hit you smack in the face, delicious! This is purely a personal thing, but I do get rather put off by the almost obligatory raindrops that seem to feature so much nowadays so for me that is the only thing that detracts but I do realise I am very much in the minority on that score. And talking of which well done for such a high one and your placing, a very creditable result Susan.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge Ooh thats nice were my words aloud as soon as it appeared! What a wonderful time of year this is, its colours and textures just have to be exploited to the full and your image does just that. I like the frame-filling aspect but its those lovely vibrant colours that hit you smack in the face, delicious! This is purely a personal thing, but I do get rather put off by the almost obligatory raindrops that seem to feature so much nowadays so for me that is the only thing that detracts but I do realise I am very much in the minority on that score. And talking of which well done for such a high one and your placing, a very creditable result Susan.', '2016-10-26 17:53:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(7479652, 1188987, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>Another lovely landscape Janine, the lighting has separated the golden foliage nicely to make it stand out. It would have made it even better if we could have seen more of the foliage in the reflection by removing the immediate foreground and a lower viewpoint. I have to agree with glads comments about sharpness there is a lack of it, its only that immediate foreground that does appear sharp which is probably why it is rather more forceful than is desirable. Having said all that the composition is good and generally a very capable image.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge Another lovely landscape Janine, the lighting has separated the golden foliage nicely to make it stand out. It would have made it even better if we could have seen more of the foliage in the reflection by removing the immediate foreground and a lower viewpoint. I have to agree with glads comments about sharpness there is a lack of it, its only that immediate foreground that does appear sharp which is probably why it is rather more forceful than is desirable. Having said all that the composition is good and generally a very capable image.', '2016-10-26 18:00:45.000000', NULL, 0),
